-The method operates on a regular cubical grid of voxels and discretizes the unit sphere of directions into $M$ bins. It solves the radiative transfer equation by iteratively propagating radiosity through these bins, using a precomputed scattering matrix for intermediate bounces and exact directions only for the source and viewer interactions [S1, book].
+The method operates on a regular cubical grid of voxels and discretizes the unit sphere of directions into $M$ bins [S1, book]. It solves the radiative transfer equation by iteratively propagating radiosity through these bins, using a precomputed scattering matrix for intermediate bounces and exact directions only for the source and viewer interactions [S1, book].
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
